  'Supply Chain Information Systems / ERP',
  'Supply Chain Information Systems / ERP teaches students how enterprise systems connect supply-chain strategy to operational execution. Students study ERP modules, master data, MRP, procure-to-pay, order-to-cash, manufacturing planning, warehouse and logistics systems, analytics, integration, cloud platforms, implementation, internal controls, cybersecurity, and digital transformation. The course is designed around practical process exercises and a capstone ERP-enabled supply-chain transformation case.',
  $scerpjson${"slug": "supply-chain-information-systems-erp", "title": "Supply Chain Information Systems / ERP", "description": "Supply Chain Information Systems / ERP teaches students how enterprise systems connect supply-chain strategy to operational execution. Students study ERP modules, master data, MRP, procure-to-pay, order-to-cash, manufacturing planning, warehouse and logistics systems, analytics, integration, cloud platforms, implementation, internal controls, cybersecurity, and digital transformation. The course is designed around practical process exercises and a capstone ERP-enabled supply-chain transformation case.", "topics": [{"id": "e56d2787-4c63-4e53-a83d-33a906b3f816", "type": "topic", "title": "Enterprise Systems and Digital Supply Chain Strategy", "description": "This opening unit explains why ERP and supply-chain systems matter: they connect planning, procurement, manufacturing, warehousing, logistics, finance, and customer service into one operating model.", "children": [{"id": "ff5c05e4-9faa-47cd-9230-0cdfc1b58139", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ERP Value and Scope", "children": [{"id": "eeeeedbc-8c79-42ab-8107-3ba9864dcc4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Single source of operational truth"}, {"id": "a2cf5a78-7a01-45a0-9258-0f3fa6684549", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-functional process integration"}, {"id": "5765c6cd-bf1a-416b-98a2-2146ff4a788e", "type": "concept", "title": "ERP, SCM suites, best-of-breed applications, and platform ecosystems"}], "description": "Students learn what ERP does for supply chains and why integration changes managerial decision making."}, {"id": "0cf23ef0-87a0-43ef-a94a-59a9c8ed1f9b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital Supply Chain Architecture", "children": [{"id": "0b8ffbc0-c7ca-4949-ad54-b52c9e5d8ad6", "type": "concept", "title": "ERP, APS, WMS, TMS, CRM, SRM, MES, PLM, BI, and data platforms"}, {"id": "829b4a93-8f9b-480d-87fc-32697fdb34fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Cloud, SaaS, on-premise, hybrid, and composable architectures"}, {"id": "129f9ca8-d712-41c8-9743-02eb18333659", "type": "concept", "title": "APIs, EDI, event streams, middleware, and integration layers"}], "description": "The goal is to see how systems fit together before learning individual modules."}, {"id": "f023684b-88ac-46bb-9997-ebc0d017dcf2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strategic Fit and Business Case", "children": [{"id": "72c4daf0-c222-4949-bb7c-8094a82fe41e", "type": "concept", "title": "Process standardization versus local flexibility"}, {"id": "3a889791-1565-4765-bc9d-61b8730b9d20", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, service, working capital, visibility, and compliance benefits"}, {"id": "0e78b8d2-e174-4dc0-8952-67baffd2b0e5", "type": "concept", "title": "ROI, total cost of ownership, and value realization"}], "description": "Students learn to connect system choices to strategy, service, cost, resilience, and growth."}]}, {"id": "5aa1b51a-6cbb-4b20-b7f0-94c3459c1e30", "type": "topic", "title": "ERP Foundations, Modules and Business Process Integration", "description": "ERP works by embedding business processes into shared modules and data structures. This unit gives students the operating map.", "children": [{"id": "237f1d75-df47-4e12-88be-80307fc4ff7a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core ERP Modules", "children": [{"id": "0d879d50-ef46-4f71-bdef-abdd5e0be1ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Materials management, sales and distribution, production planning, warehouse management, finance, controlling, quality, and maintenance"}, {"id": "4a2131ad-7040-45fd-b7e7-c1cb916e81c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Module boundaries and handoffs"}, {"id": "9b052853-f9cd-4732-befb-c190e08b3656", "type": "concept", "title": "Transaction, master, and configuration data"}], "description": "Students learn the major ERP modules and the supply-chain work each supports."}, {"id": "5cee4b14-fc2b-4731-950f-bda863fb5ed5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Process Integration", "children": [{"id": "71b03f6b-f4b3-4bab-899c-805b3805c5e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Procurement to inventory to accounts payable"}, {"id": "ab7a6260-6a79-42b9-8269-3c7a65d28028", "type": "concept", "title": "Sales order to delivery to billing to receivables"}, {"id": "b803fc87-42f4-42ba-9c83-0192cf97f04f", "type": "concept", "title": "Production planning to shop-floor confirmation to inventory and costing"}], "description": "The point is to understand how one transaction triggers downstream operational and financial effects."}, {"id": "84791b65-e89e-47e6-bf32-43b32150b345", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ERP User Experience", "children": [{"id": "622344d8-a4d5-4647-8d7b-bcebf96b92bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Role-based interfaces, dashboards, workflows, approvals, and alerts"}, {"id": "a6b29035-16d1-42b9-bd84-559995818a68", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobile, Fiori-style, and low-code experiences"}, {"id": "77baf6e0-66c9-47ce-8c95-b2f4c414a900", "type": "concept", "title": "Usability, training, and adoption barriers"}], "description": "Students learn how users interact with modern ERP systems."}]}, {"id": "81f4fd55-3f59-4bab-98aa-7b40ea39f580", "type": "topic", "title": "Business Process Modeling and Systems Analysis", "description": "A good ERP course needs process thinking. Students learn how to map current work, design future work, and translate process needs into system requirements.", "children": [{"id": "9c705460-fdea-4603-a56b-ccd2fcdcb1ec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Process Modeling", "children": [{"id": "37090ac7-1e8d-4387-99c8-e73ab6c21c37", "type": "concept", "title": "BPMN, swimlanes, SIPOC, value-stream maps, and process decomposition"}, {"id": "cd2d2b69-8a62-4abe-acf4-c369ff346e2f", "type": "concept", "title": "As-is and to-be models"}, {"id": "66c2e67f-0dc1-4314-98ae-9ec91b2ef52c", "type": "concept", "title": "Exceptions, handoffs, bottlenecks, and control points"}], "description": "Students learn visual tools for making supply-chain processes explicit."}, {"id": "37c61767-e45c-436c-9614-0718d2d92b4f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Requirements and Fit-Gap Analysis", "children": [{"id": "8c9e1e02-8275-4d9f-b8d7-ac5de3d15b68", "type": "concept", "title": "Functional, data, reporting, security, and integration requirements"}, {"id": "82efc616-1756-4c9f-a1eb-fbe09d6bbebb", "type": "concept", "title": "Fit-gap workshops and acceptance criteria"}, {"id": "3aff225e-c572-4034-af45-0d45e213e1b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Standard process adoption versus customization"}], "description": "The goal is to decide where a system fits, where process changes are needed, and where configuration or extensions are justified."}, {"id": "62690b8a-818b-41ad-8d08-2ebc27f9f91f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Process Governance", "children": [{"id": "74adb2de-6838-417d-a422-adbcd0e6e1e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Process owners, data owners, super users, and IT partners"}, {"id": "6d3b5d36-dfcc-4fee-9251-b2bff9b8ed69", "type": "concept", "title": "Change control and design authority"}, {"id": "45b57dc8-b3fc-4859-90d8-4db3e2c865cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation, training, and continuous improvement"}], "description": "Students learn that enterprise systems require process ownership and decision rights."}]}, {"id": "14473478-e90c-4b11-9059-b21507d41afb", "type": "topic", "title": "Master Data Management and Data Governance", "description": "ERP quality depends on data quality. This topic teaches the data structures and governance disciplines that keep supply-chain processes reliable.", "children": [{"id": "b33b16a1-b4e1-451c-9fdd-f7fe0aa2b4eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supply Chain Master Data", "children": [{"id": "17a5f459-23c5-4c72-a14b-66de8be3a5b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Material, item, SKU, vendor, customer, plant, warehouse, location, work center, routing, and BOM"}, {"id": "7ffc24b1-f720-469f-b84c-9f5b2c5bc776", "type": "concept", "title": "Units of measure, lead times, sourcing rules, prices, and tax data"}, {"id": "b0ae9af6-f39e-4e17-a80e-8e2f66408ee8", "type": "concept", "title": "Data dependencies across modules"}], "description": "Students learn the master records that drive planning, execution, and finance."}, {"id": "ef37c226-86e0-44a5-a5f3-80dcf70b2df0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data Quality and Stewardship", "children": [{"id": "e8b09fe6-41fa-45da-a341-40992723175c", "type": "concept", "title": "Completeness, accuracy, timeliness, uniqueness, and consistency"}, {"id": "292a8ebe-57c0-4bd3-b64c-ba41a53c56aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Data owners, stewards, approval workflows, and data lifecycle"}, {"id": "1ef4c734-ce16-4b69-b3b4-651decb3586c", "type": "concept", "title": "Duplicate, obsolete, and conflicting records"}], "description": "The point is to prevent bad data from becoming bad operations."}, {"id": "80342ffc-21ff-41f4-b049-cddbc18d1d93", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Governance and Controls", "children": [{"id": "e1ad9f52-ae2d-4250-918b-a8099a27389d", "type": "concept", "title": "Master data policies and standards"}, {"id": "cc90f16f-77f1-4e99-9a57-e7d7d9d4c3e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Change logs, approvals, and segregation of duties"}, {"id": "feb5d890-720f-4b2c-b0ee-36126f063332", "type": "concept", "title": "Data lineage, metadata, and audit readiness"}], "description": "Students learn how governance makes data trustworthy and auditable."}]}, {"id": "0597f46f-6e2e-4793-bbb2-fd0f8e5393da", "type": "topic", "title": "Material Requirements Planning and Supply Planning Logic", "description": "MRP is one of the classic supply-chain uses of ERP. Students learn how demand, BOMs, inventory, and lead times become planned orders.", "children": [{"id": "c97e9fcb-1e3e-4848-bad9-4667a629097b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "MRP Inputs", "children": [{"id": "da163b7b-9dd8-4a6c-bbd1-b07e026edde5", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand forecasts, customer orders, BOMs, inventory balances, scheduled receipts, and lead times"}, {"id": "63682792-b874-4e05-87f7-7694b837dcb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning calendars, lot sizes, safety stock, and sourcing rules"}, {"id": "41dca6b2-f1db-44e9-aae2-3e340c00cb82", "type": "concept", "title": "Data errors and planning nervousness"}], "description": "Students learn what information the planning engine needs before it can produce useful recommendations."}, {"id": "01cb0db9-8d03-441b-8bb6-d5669b365e26", "type": "subtopic", "title": "MRP Calculations", "children": [{"id": "ea948860-916b-4c9f-a894-4024a543e322", "type": "concept", "title": "Net requirements, BOM explosion, time phasing, offsetting, and pegging"}, {"id": "49156f3c-b690-42b8-a134-1dc16e7cf779", "type": "concept", "title": "Planned orders, purchase requisitions, production orders, and exception messages"}, {"id": "2ad2c701-a27a-4a3c-86c3-8d05118e8e3f", "type": "concept", "title": "MRP versus DRP and multi-echelon planning"}], "description": "The goal is to understand the planning logic rather than treat ERP output as magic."}, {"id": "0db175e8-0a87-4241-a8e0-5703c5e6f7c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Planner Decision Making", "children": [{"id": "22d783c3-7605-4121-a1ef-2a63d3b156ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Expedite, defer, cancel, and reschedule messages"}, {"id": "1a85dd3b-b0b8-4ba2-921a-0810f5e825a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Shortages, excess, substitutions, and capacity checks"}, {"id": "ef478689-51a9-4072-8b8b-d07bf9b63ce5", "type": "concept", "title": "Planner workbenches and exception-based planning"}], "description": "Students learn how planners interpret and override system suggestions."}]}, {"id": "1ea362d0-cd77-4f2a-8d13-55ed1f97986e", "type": "topic", "title": "Procure-to-Pay and Supplier Integration", "description": "Procure-to-pay connects sourcing, buying, receiving, inventory, quality, and finance. Students learn the end-to-end process and the controls around it.", "children": [{"id": "fa97a213-d90a-40fc-a1d9-e3bf8a0a51ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "P2P Workflow", "children": [{"id": "5daa4048-31f1-483e-a1f8-67d858f4c324", "type": "concept", "title": "Purchase requisition, purchase order, approval, goods receipt, quality inspection, invoice receipt, and payment"}, {"id": "6a5ba963-6784-4294-8b05-4381bcacd668", "type": "concept", "title": "Three-way match and tolerance management"}, {"id": "ae7f245c-309f-4948-85e6-6d9f300b5173", "type": "concept", "title": "Service procurement and indirect spend variants"}], "description": "Students learn the standard transaction chain from need to payment."}, {"id": "e82dcc79-f828-4733-b7c7-121365c7b005", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supplier Collaboration", "children": [{"id": "c94bb48a-644a-4625-a223-6f8cb1252621", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier portals, EDI, ASN, order acknowledgment, and vendor-managed inventory"}, {"id": "4dc234a9-6fe9-4649-85e6-303543a6cafd", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier scorecards and compliance documentation"}, {"id": "1fa1e534-3596-4363-bf03-2eb7a6a788ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Catalogs, contracts, and e-procurement"}], "description": "The point is to understand how ERP extends across organizational boundaries."}, {"id": "232090b4-9393-4ba4-958f-2e0ade0d955a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Controls and Risks", "children": [{"id": "6aede2ba-03f3-478a-ad8b-b2dbd862bd27", "type": "concept", "title": "Unauthorized purchases, duplicate payments, price variance, receipt errors, and fraud"}, {"id": "61b1c4d7-9ba2-4917-8cc6-8f85454646a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Approval matrices, delegation of authority, and audit trails"}, {"id": "2facf4a4-5716-4dd5-ab04-2ddf037aff75", "type": "concept", "title": "Segregation of duties among request, approve, receive, and pay"}], "description": "Students learn why P2P is a major internal-control area."}]}, {"id": "0593b1ff-691c-4d4e-9f0e-f75933f6a59a", "type": "topic", "title": "Order-to-Cash, Customer Fulfillment and Service", "description": "Order-to-cash links demand capture, availability, logistics, billing, and customer service. It is where ERP touches revenue and customer experience.", "children": [{"id": "c2e15f42-b4ef-44df-b60c-81338ff5a69d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "O2C Workflow", "children": [{"id": "ec653aca-ea35-4e99-9ce5-7b7056eff08c", "type": "concept", "title": "Quote, sales order, credit check, ATP, pick, pack, ship, invoice, and cash application"}, {"id": "382b191a-7628-4fd1-a52f-1bcd5116d495", "type": "concept", "title": "Backorders, substitutions, allocations, and delivery blocks"}, {"id": "12add95d-89bb-44ba-9275-455a00420562", "type": "concept", "title": "Returns, claims, and customer service cases"}], "description": "Students learn the end-to-end order process."}, {"id": "fb72b25a-01c3-4440-87a0-ecd6857dc31d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Availability and Fulfillment", "children": [{"id": "e3e4526f-35c6-401a-8b99-22c9e6da755b", "type": "concept", "title": "Available-to-promise, capable-to-promise, allocation, and reservation logic"}, {"id": "e97c6207-0726-451d-9760-77a196f6cc92", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer priority, service levels, and channel rules"}, {"id": "c83d42d3-0318-4f84-9114-dd79e1620eac", "type": "concept", "title": "Warehouse and transportation execution links"}], "description": "The focus is how system logic determines what customers can be promised."}, {"id": "1a7eaeaa-3df1-4180-a795-a760a6db4551", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revenue and Control Touchpoints", "children": [{"id": "c615c899-ec65-423d-bcad-6bf23d1771d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Billing, taxes, rebates, revenue recognition touchpoints, and credit management"}, {"id": "ee1ca0a5-37dc-4f90-ba5c-2609965c6157", "type": "concept", "title": "Order holds, pricing conditions, and discount approvals"}, {"id": "7279b493-7cd4-41f8-b633-d7bd9f13c55d", "type": "concept", "title": "Audit trail from order to cash"}], "description": "Students learn how operational transactions connect to financial results."}]}, {"id": "5df039eb-bfab-4f0a-a505-dd9f9642ecce", "type": "topic", "title": "Manufacturing Planning, MES and Quality Integration", "description": "ERP supports manufacturing by connecting materials, capacity, production, quality, and costing. Students learn how planning becomes shop-floor execution.", "children": [{"id": "3be416fb-d985-4f9a-bf98-75167845293f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Production Planning", "children": [{"id": "23b17e50-2d9d-4e7b-9f77-f769db16a858", "type": "concept", "title": "MPS, MRP, routings, work centers, capacity, and production orders"}, {"id": "29fcf0a0-659e-4249-9892-f5c6e8609cc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Make-to-stock, make-to-order, assemble-to-order, and engineer-to-order"}, {"id": "14decd0e-b2a5-4023-b8be-a07d9fb0840d", "type": "concept", "title": "Finite versus infinite capacity and constraint visibility"}], "description": "Students learn the planning structures used in manufacturing environments."}, {"id": "bd432a90-c80d-4c8e-a64d-053e8f0716d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shop-Floor Execution", "children": [{"id": "b1957c6f-6c7b-40d8-9451-1f08fb2fbdf7", "type": "concept", "title": "MES, confirmations, labor, machine time, scrap, yield, and downtime"}, {"id": "87724539-b428-4a73-a783-45ede520ea38", "type": "concept", "title": "Component issue, backflush, and finished-goods receipt"}, {"id": "34845180-ac42-4583-9e9a-0306bfc07a1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Traceability and genealogy"}], "description": "The point is to understand how production data flows back into the enterprise system."}, {"id": "b0f3d034-140d-4601-bfe5-b498cef300f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quality and Cost Integration", "children": [{"id": "eb48d7a2-ea59-47a2-b0ba-4c5cd6bb94e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Inspection lots, nonconformance, corrective action, and holds"}, {"id": "35e3a560-e4b0-459d-9781-b20f0baf00d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Standard cost, variance, work-in-process, and production settlement"}, {"id": "5ef6d953-69bb-43c6-809a-11a72cbbd4cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality data for suppliers and customers"}], "description": "Students see how quality and costing are embedded in operational flows."}]}, {"id": "dedb1242-a27b-404c-9a5a-81438069b8ea", "type": "topic", "title": "Warehouse, Inventory and Logistics Systems", "description": "ERP supply-chain execution depends on warehouse and logistics systems. This topic connects WMS, TMS, inventory accuracy, and physical flow.", "children": [{"id": "d0aa0d7a-dd36-4613-be82-1c1c6ecc4603", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Warehouse Management Systems", "children": [{"id": "b15c136d-785b-4eaa-bca7-11d742de554b", "type": "concept", "title": "Receiving, putaway, slotting, replenishment, picking, packing, shipping, and cycle counting"}, {"id": "cebe48ca-5527-4485-b3a3-484fdccea4cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Barcode, RFID, mobile scanning, automation, and labor management"}, {"id": "1bb04dea-305b-4e4f-a5c7-f4c8fd01120e", "type": "concept", "title": "Warehouse tasking and exception handling"}], "description": "Students learn how WMS functionality supports execution."}, {"id": "b0eec975-23fd-4ef1-8d34-a34917f57a19", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory Accuracy and Visibility", "children": [{"id": "c7d8e007-36ce-401e-b3bb-37937aa9ef73", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory status, batch, serial, lot, bin, and location control"}, {"id": "edfc909c-031e-4937-bc85-a253ebe1eac3", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle counting, adjustments, reconciliation, and shrink"}, {"id": "e71d7311-693a-4c77-b412-481a510dc609", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory valuation and financial impact"}], "description": "The goal is to connect system inventory to physical inventory."}, {"id": "1c5a9f70-4cac-4c6f-a500-7a316e2ad146", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transportation and Yard Integration", "children": [{"id": "75d1e8b7-0a62-430c-b846-ba5fce8a9dc9", "type": "concept", "title": "TMS rating, tendering, shipment planning, tracking, freight audit, and claims"}, {"id": "639cea45-1dbb-4733-ac1a-5a2b3e92cd93", "type": "concept", "title": "Yard management, dock appointments, and trailer visibility"}, {"id": "b1c025e7-8c41-4af8-a446-ebce22eab432", "type": "concept", "title": "Carrier EDI/API and shipment event data"}], "description": "Students learn how logistics systems connect to ERP and WMS."}]}, {"id": "c1693132-51cd-4d12-aea5-8d9bb067736e", "type": "topic", "title": "ERP Analytics, BI and Supply Chain Control Towers", "description": "Systems are valuable only when they produce useful decisions. This section teaches reporting, dashboards, KPIs, and control-tower thinking.", "children": [{"id": "983c358a-4263-4b86-ab02-8972979f6267", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Operational Reporting", "children": [{"id": "efa4cad6-80ca-4576-a2f1-d474a42ccee2", "type": "concept", "title": "Open orders, inventory, shortages, aging, supplier performance, delivery performance, and exceptions"}, {"id": "dd0b8bde-eaac-4d93-b5d2-f1af8691d67a", "type": "concept", "title": "Embedded analytics and self-service BI"}, {"id": "3bde1eb7-6da3-4127-9b44-a3cd9d066683", "type": "concept", "title": "Report governance and metric definitions"}], "description": "Students learn the difference between transaction reports, management reports, and analytical views."}, {"id": "48de6c08-25eb-4554-9fe5-333ea4cfefc4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supply Chain KPIs", "children": [{"id": "53a746c0-8dcb-49c5-b392-0f3d375db369", "type": "concept", "title": "OTIF, fill rate, forecast accuracy, inventory turns, days of supply, schedule adherence, procurement savings, and order cycle time"}, {"id": "fedcc45f-2dc4-4b4f-88ec-b244c91d1245", "type": "concept", "title": "Leading versus lagging indicators"}, {"id": "e239bca6-97ca-4068-b9e9-2054dd9a680b", "type": "concept", "title": "KPI ownership, thresholds, and review cadence"}], "description": "The point is to choose measures that support action."}, {"id": "cbd07e64-7698-4fdf-9b6a-28dbe7eb0612", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Control Towers and Decision Support", "children": [{"id": "aeb6958d-833f-4edb-9e5b-4dc6eb265b42", "type": "concept", "title": "Visibility platforms, event management, alerts, predictive ETA, and risk signals"}, {"id": "05305b0b-6e6b-4412-9c2b-816e16cac410", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario analysis and what-if planning"}, {"id": "2e485e9f-79a9-4fe1-af08-e7455d3c504e", "type": "concept", "title": "Decision rights and escalation workflows"}], "description": "Students learn how integrated data supports real-time coordination."}]}, {"id": "d042a3ba-8b97-48f6-bd8c-bf6bcc026a99", "type": "topic", "title": "Integration, APIs, EDI and Platform Architecture", "description": "Supply-chain systems rarely stand alone. Students learn how ERP connects to partners, platforms, machines, and analytics environments.", "children": [{"id": "49bf130e-2722-462e-8a2e-bcdde71fa1da", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integration Patterns", "children": [{"id": "de6e22c9-bdec-4372-8147-3f027565c401", "type": "concept", "title": "Batch, real-time, API, EDI, file transfer, message queues, and event streams"}, {"id": "93464402-9cab-4af8-9e8b-46a45d15eeea", "type": "concept", "title": "Point-to-point versus middleware and iPaaS"}, {"id": "5219f643-ec0f-47c9-b0b4-0ec5e6dcbafe", "type": "concept", "title": "Canonical data models and mapping"}], "description": "Students learn the common ways enterprise systems exchange data."}, {"id": "ae14ae94-c256-4cb5-8105-f65ecc82e691", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Partner and Ecosystem Integration", "children": [{"id": "b9f98353-8eac-4a01-b6de-90f9188fb232", "type": "concept", "title": "Purchase orders, ASNs, invoices, forecasts, inventory, shipment status, and remittance data"}, {"id": "335553c8-3791-4902-ba0d-9642b725be6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier portals, customer portals, and logistics platforms"}, {"id": "9e95a6a9-d4ae-4b5e-8941-c6aa0155e36f", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards, testing, and onboarding"}], "description": "The focus is on supplier, customer, carrier, and marketplace connections."}, {"id": "2d824e26-86e3-4369-b1d1-a9fa23369b92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Architecture Risks", "children": [{"id": "343377d3-cba8-40bd-93f0-366e95d46313", "type": "concept", "title": "Latency, failed messages, duplicates, reconciliation, and error handling"}, {"id": "8cca5d1b-5022-4644-bcaa-0354dda85952", "type": "concept", "title": "Interface monitoring, logging, retry logic, and support ownership"}, {"id": "9d672831-ee6b-4da7-a081-b96885a124cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Security, authentication, authorization, and data exposure"}], "description": "Students learn why integration design affects reliability and cyber risk."}]}, {"id": "280d310b-c5a6-4323-a6dc-41858ee47d9a", "type": "topic", "title": "Cloud ERP, SaaS and Digital Supply Chain Platforms", "description": "Enterprise systems increasingly run in cloud and SaaS environments. Students learn the architectural, operational, and strategic implications.", "children": [{"id": "a9e0d2d6-54ea-49b5-860f-a5adfe12aa1e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cloud ERP Models", "children": [{"id": "d69de76a-4fc0-4c79-bbad-503821403264", "type": "concept", "title": "Public cloud, private cloud, hybrid, SaaS, and managed services"}, {"id": "43c53cc7-5723-4e3c-92a9-b00573c0ba7c", "type": "concept", "title": "SAP S/4HANA Cloud, Oracle Cloud ERP/SCM, Dynamics 365, NetSuite, and best-of-breed platforms"}, {"id": "e7cddcca-20d9-4dd3-90ca-58213944a994", "type": "concept", "title": "Upgrade cadence, extensibility, and vendor lock-in"}], "description": "Students compare deployment models and their trade-offs."}, {"id": "0d4f52b5-d369-4c51-bed6-4705c8236ba6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Platform Capabilities", "children": [{"id": "fabb06ed-eb90-4b91-94e7-bddde00e7a2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Workflow automation, low-code apps, process mining, embedded analytics, AI services, and integration services"}, {"id": "deb22b3b-1314-4a49-96a1-543e1e1e247f", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobile, role-based, and API-first design"}, {"id": "c272b271-91bd-4f8b-94c8-335c13b0b996", "type": "concept", "title": "Data lakes, lakehouses, and operational data stores"}], "description": "The goal is to see modern ERP as a platform, not just a transaction system."}, {"id": "279a5f0a-ae5a-4d32-9092-3983f9867e21", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cloud Operations", "children": [{"id": "2452c097-c8f5-4127-a742-2f548454d44e", "type": "concept", "title": "Availability, backup, disaster recovery, observability, and incident management"}, {"id": "708ce793-8c5d-41c9-839d-2ab1c37a2d06", "type": "concept", "title": "Identity, access, and environment management"}, {"id": "bd20dcd1-90d0-47ab-9f30-a7e6db28e182", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost management, licensing, and service-level agreements"}], "description": "Students learn operational disciplines for cloud enterprise systems."}]}, {"id": "e33f1253-5952-49c5-b497-294cce54fd2f", "type": "topic", "title": "ERP Implementation, Project Governance and Change Management", "description": "ERP implementation is a business transformation project. This topic teaches the governance, delivery, testing, and adoption work needed for success.", "children": [{"id": "b1f44fc0-e4f1-4c25-982f-071dee9c2591", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Implementation Life Cycle", "children": [{"id": "5ca5359c-75bf-43bb-99d9-9ff4c41c5f54", "type": "concept", "title": "Discovery, blueprint/design, build, test, deploy, stabilize, and optimize"}, {"id": "5a8ccbd7-6cfb-44c4-9010-966573d616e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Waterfall, agile, hybrid, and fit-to-standard approaches"}, {"id": "d3423b67-000e-487b-8f22-efd049cc59b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Project charter, scope, plan, RAID log, and governance structure"}], "description": "Students learn major delivery phases and artifacts."}, {"id": "66563a68-b3f7-42e4-8c43-73d13056268d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Testing and Cutover", "children": [{"id": "d50a1fdd-2a95-43f2-a216-93b24d264baa", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit, integration, user acceptance, regression, performance, and security testing"}, {"id": "8de41696-7aee-4e08-90d8-2d7af7b44133", "type": "concept", "title": "Mock cutovers, data migration rehearsal, and go/no-go criteria"}, {"id": "db17852e-6c06-4d9f-b9f9-b9e99e3daa9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Hypercare, issue triage, and stabilization"}], "description": "The point is to reduce go-live risk through disciplined validation."}, {"id": "8cc13fe8-e4a2-4f19-917e-7165a361af5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Organizational Change", "children": [{"id": "1ba054de-48bb-40e9-ad38-444584133823", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder analysis, communication, training, super-user networks, and resistance management"}, {"id": "ff02cca4-c540-4226-b04e-ac8ee9a6a3c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Role redesign and process ownership"}, {"id": "2cfd5072-b9d4-4015-9b11-f65fa886a6bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefits tracking and value realization"}], "description": "Students learn why user adoption is as important as system configuration."}]}, {"id": "195b242f-1932-4534-b2cf-d64b78eb0047", "type": "topic", "title": "Data Migration, Testing and ERP Process Labs", "description": "Hands-on process exercises make ERP concrete. Students learn to move data, execute transactions, and validate end-to-end flows.", "children": [{"id": "ad8c5353-8f22-429a-a9fb-c92105de7917", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data Migration", "children": [{"id": "a5e6ef60-7ca3-45a2-9963-709e6a98a7bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Extract, cleanse, transform, load, validate, and reconcile"}, {"id": "f76a791c-404b-4be3-8251-1da86f7c4dc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Master data, open transactions, balances, and historical data"}, {"id": "c6a91fd5-846b-486d-a45b-d312825c6e50", "type": "concept", "title": "Migration defects and remediation"}], "description": "Students learn the practical discipline of moving legacy data into ERP."}, {"id": "4762a56f-ae71-4b68-b011-d4517206f051", "type": "subtopic", "title": "End-to-End Process Labs", "children": [{"id": "83e0ea4a-b3b8-46a5-b2dc-be75d24038d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Material creation, purchase order, goods receipt, invoice, sales order, delivery, and billing"}, {"id": "289c2c7f-5fd2-4455-9230-dd96329af75a", "type": "concept", "title": "MRP run, production order, warehouse task, and inventory count"}, {"id": "af50505d-b3cb-4f27-993d-50f726f87902", "type": "concept", "title": "Error diagnosis and exception resolution"}], "description": "The goal is to practice processes as integrated workflows."}, {"id": "94b477e2-ee33-4a0a-80e1-ce4bb5f61e5a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Test Evidence and Documentation", "children": [{"id": "6b7b8342-ffbb-40a6-88e6-4a4636c21a88", "type": "concept", "title": "Test scripts, test data, defects, retesting, approvals, and evidence"}, {"id": "71ce401e-a01b-4790-b5dd-60c3c278a9ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Traceability from requirements to tests"}, {"id": "529f1da5-9244-4e27-b132-c42e8e91e091", "type": "concept", "title": "Standard operating procedures and training aids"}], "description": "Students learn how ERP teams prove readiness."}]}, {"id": "39124d22-9b28-414a-980d-3f97e2ddcb7d", "type": "topic", "title": "Internal Controls, Segregation of Duties and Auditability", "description": "ERP systems sit at the heart of operational and financial controls. Students learn how controls are designed, monitored, and audited.", "children": [{"id": "be0c2017-4d3e-43eb-8f11-d146ce8b583a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Access and Authorization", "children": [{"id": "9704218b-5e34-4234-a3ab-8551b5538367", "type": "concept", "title": "Role-based access control, least privilege, privileged access, and emergency access"}, {"id": "dc36b30e-2122-4d2e-8b64-7fcd0557e408", "type": "concept", "title": "User provisioning, approval, review, and termination"}, {"id": "6339a451-336e-4dd4-8836-ce4eb9266cc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Authentication, MFA, and identity integration"}], "description": "Students learn the control logic behind user roles and permissions."}, {"id": "f1cd4295-aed2-4816-ade4-f5470742b203", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Segregation of Duties", "children": [{"id": "cc950ffb-1bf4-4633-abd9-07b485b6ba1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Create vendor and pay vendor"}, {"id": "5748e22d-e616-4b18-8847-6b67b738c54d", "type": "concept", "title": "Create purchase order and approve receipt"}, {"id": "e6b14efb-971d-4fb0-a97f-ecce9e0730f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Create customer, approve credit, and issue refund"}], "description": "The focus is on preventing risky combinations of access."}, {"id": "3a170aa0-c104-43f1-8e0c-5f002d70a763", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audit and Compliance", "children": [{"id": "12a53e6c-0122-4bb4-89fd-50bff84a97d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Change logs, workflow approvals, transaction trails, and configuration records"}, {"id": "b388f303-b456-477a-af81-fdc566f66685", "type": "concept", "title": "SOX-style controls, IT general controls, and application controls"}, {"id": "b2e37f01-51c6-459a-acd3-5bd4d781a2bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuous controls monitoring"}], "description": "Students learn how ERP evidence supports internal and external assurance."}]}, {"id": "9568433e-05e8-426f-9467-b907d055c64c", "type": "topic", "title": "Cybersecurity, Privacy and Supply Chain Technology Risk", "description": "Enterprise systems create cyber and operational risk. This unit teaches security and risk management for ERP and connected supply-chain platforms.", "children": [{"id": "8a6d8512-9250-44e2-956e-0d6ec05e07ef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ERP Security Threats", "children": [{"id": "95698935-0b9b-4cf2-83ae-c8eb5f5e4fcc", "type": "concept", "title": "Credential compromise, privilege abuse, ransomware, data exfiltration, interface abuse, and third-party compromise"}, {"id": "bad87ae6-af70-4833-9150-2fb1a3d1fd7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Misconfiguration, unpatched systems, insecure APIs, and shadow integrations"}, {"id": "c7e03bfe-d92e-4dbd-b6dd-c716c039da39", "type": "concept", "title": "Business interruption and fraud risk"}], "description": "Students learn common risk scenarios in enterprise systems."}, {"id": "50ae17ed-1ffa-4dd7-8616-50a923654137", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cyber Supply Chain Risk Management", "children": [{"id": "0e7ab1f1-3799-4c26-9737-4c523080bf26", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier assurance, software risk, vendor access, and dependency mapping"}, {"id": "8cd37fa6-c7da-4bda-825c-f0581c8d1178", "type": "concept", "title": "Contractual security requirements and monitoring"}, {"id": "6b516dbe-9c2c-434a-9730-dee439ad2b0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident response and resilience planning"}], "description": "The goal is to apply frameworks such as NIST SP 800-161 to supplier and technology ecosystems."}, {"id": "a7cf8782-a074-4cd7-b52f-1117c5799b8c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Privacy and Data Protection", "children": [{"id": "f55d9713-c513-40fa-8502-f3608003738d", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer, employee, supplier, and payment data"}, {"id": "6db05f6a-19b0-4ab2-b935-66040c509278", "type": "concept", "title": "Data minimization, retention, masking, encryption, and lawful use"}, {"id": "d4ee44e3-19b7-4cf8-a5d2-926139d417ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-border data and compliance considerations"}], "description": "Students learn how personal and sensitive data must be governed in ERP contexts."}]}, {"id": "dc4ff381-d027-468d-9a80-05415e9b4e04", "type": "topic", "title": "Advanced Planning, AI, IoT and Automation in ERP-Enabled Supply Chains", "description": "Modern supply chains combine ERP with advanced planning, AI, IoT, automation, and digital twins. This topic prepares students for the next layer of systems capability.", "children": [{"id": "5d195183-9918-4908-948e-8322d4c07b47", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Advanced Planning Systems", "children": [{"id": "7a3e6896-a42a-4d4b-a5e6-c6ae1a6634aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand planning, supply planning, S&OP, inventory optimization, and allocation"}, {"id": "b45d4d48-cdcd-4214-b69e-bf42b9e6f89f", "type": "concept", "title": "Constraint-based planning and scenario simulation"}, {"id": "e9c14794-6b92-4d70-be59-3e9bbcb30155", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning master data and integration to execution"}], "description": "Students learn how planning systems extend core ERP."}, {"id": "9743a002-97c6-401c-9d47-3875d19aefc9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AI and Predictive Analytics", "children": [{"id": "5cf6d623-258a-47bd-b80e-457e772371d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Forecasting, anomaly detection, ETA prediction, supplier risk, and recommendation engines"}, {"id": "feb4efb0-4e1e-42a5-9943-58938d30972c", "type": "concept", "title": "Model evaluation, bias, explainability, and human oversight"}, {"id": "9a1c2a56-8f54-4ba5-b80d-47f19f616db4", "type": "concept", "title": "Operationalizing analytics into workflows"}], "description": "The point is to understand useful AI applications and their data requirements."}, {"id": "ad16c1c3-a381-4292-93cd-e4338b84d77a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IoT and Automation", "children": [{"id": "6716ea7a-45c5-46e3-bde3-de3cf2d684cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensors, RFID, telematics, robotics, automated storage, and machine data"}, {"id": "629ef220-97ed-4a4a-988b-e7e11aab93ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital twins and real-time asset visibility"}, {"id": "c212388f-95dc-4698-ac76-178b5809e50f", "type": "concept", "title": "Automation governance, safety, and exception handling"}], "description": "Students learn how physical operations generate digital signals."}]}, {"id": "c6705bbd-d9f9-4bf1-b36d-5a7a32440123", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone ERP Process Exercise and Digital Transformation Case", "description": "The course ends with a practical ERP-enabled supply-chain case. Students diagnose a process, configure or simulate the flow, analyze data, and recommend a transformation plan.", "children": [{"id": "620c54dc-f061-491c-95ae-a6fb9b245e29", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case Diagnosis", "children": [{"id": "bc75508b-0b19-427b-bc71-c195eaa6efc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Process map, pain points, data issues, controls, integrations, and stakeholders"}, {"id": "1fb4d44b-8da4-4a69-bd80-d0625a076e97", "type": "concept", "title": "Current-state performance and risk evidence"}, {"id": "fbed6276-167a-4f4e-9c79-4fde3a95ca6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Decision criteria and scope boundaries"}], "description": "Students begin by identifying the business problem and system/process constraints."}, {"id": "2f3d4233-c898-4170-803d-309a881eced3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Solution Design", "children": [{"id": "4fcf8ab7-65cd-432a-bd8f-f889ff5d915a", "type": "concept", "title": "To-be process, system roles, master data changes, integration needs, dashboards, and controls"}, {"id": "4460458c-0683-4801-94b1-cd005438519a", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation plan, training, testing, cutover, and change management"}, {"id": "71ca9e6c-8fb6-4238-95d4-deceebaf1092", "type": "concept", "title": "Cybersecurity, governance, and data-quality considerations"}], "description": "The capstone asks students to design an integrated, realistic improvement."}, {"id": "a2924bd5-44a3-483c-92c5-cb520d604e87", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Executive Recommendation", "children": [{"id": "05989c7c-d4e0-44b1-84b8-e99fc0aadf37", "type": "concept", "title": "Business case, expected benefits, risk mitigation, timeline, and operating model"}, {"id": "87fedeff-bce7-45e9-a4c5-119ab2cfc5d2", "type": "concept", "title": "KPI dashboard and value realization plan"}, {"id": "72889d23-9138-4102-a2df-ecadf353c9b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Lessons learned from the ERP process exercise"}], "description": "Students present a decision-ready transformation argument."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$scerpjson$::jsonb,
  true,
  false,
  'course',
  'public'
where not exists (
  select 1 from public.learning_paths where slug = 'supply-chain-information-systems-erp'
);

update public.learning_paths
set
  title = 'Supply Chain Information Systems / ERP',
  goal = 'Supply Chain Information Systems / ERP',
  summary = 'Supply Chain Information Systems / ERP teaches students how enterprise systems connect supply-chain strategy to operational execution. Students study ERP modules, master data, MRP, procure-to-pay, order-to-cash, manufacturing planning, warehouse and logistics systems, analytics, integration, cloud platforms, implementation, internal controls, cybersecurity, and digital transformation. The course is designed around practical process exercises and a capstone ERP-enabled supply-chain transformation case.',
  data = $scerpjson${"slug": "supply-chain-information-systems-erp", "title": "Supply Chain Information Systems / ERP", "description": "Supply Chain Information Systems / ERP teaches students how enterprise systems connect supply-chain strategy to operational execution. Students study ERP modules, master data, MRP, procure-to-pay, order-to-cash, manufacturing planning, warehouse and logistics systems, analytics, integration, cloud platforms, implementation, internal controls, cybersecurity, and digital transformation. The course is designed around practical process exercises and a capstone ERP-enabled supply-chain transformation case.", "topics": [{"id": "e56d2787-4c63-4e53-a83d-33a906b3f816", "type": "topic", "title": "Enterprise Systems and Digital Supply Chain Strategy", "description": "This opening unit explains why ERP and supply-chain systems matter: they connect planning, procurement, manufacturing, warehousing, logistics, finance, and customer service into one operating model.", "children": [{"id": "ff5c05e4-9faa-47cd-9230-0cdfc1b58139", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ERP Value and Scope", "children": [{"id": "eeeeedbc-8c79-42ab-8107-3ba9864dcc4e", "type": "concept", "title": "Single source of operational truth"}, {"id": "a2cf5a78-7a01-45a0-9258-0f3fa6684549", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-functional process integration"}, {"id": "5765c6cd-bf1a-416b-98a2-2146ff4a788e", "type": "concept", "title": "ERP, SCM suites, best-of-breed applications, and platform ecosystems"}], "description": "Students learn what ERP does for supply chains and why integration changes managerial decision making."}, {"id": "0cf23ef0-87a0-43ef-a94a-59a9c8ed1f9b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Digital Supply Chain Architecture", "children": [{"id": "0b8ffbc0-c7ca-4949-ad54-b52c9e5d8ad6", "type": "concept", "title": "ERP, APS, WMS, TMS, CRM, SRM, MES, PLM, BI, and data platforms"}, {"id": "829b4a93-8f9b-480d-87fc-32697fdb34fc", "type": "concept", "title": "Cloud, SaaS, on-premise, hybrid, and composable architectures"}, {"id": "129f9ca8-d712-41c8-9743-02eb18333659", "type": "concept", "title": "APIs, EDI, event streams, middleware, and integration layers"}], "description": "The goal is to see how systems fit together before learning individual modules."}, {"id": "f023684b-88ac-46bb-9997-ebc0d017dcf2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Strategic Fit and Business Case", "children": [{"id": "72c4daf0-c222-4949-bb7c-8094a82fe41e", "type": "concept", "title": "Process standardization versus local flexibility"}, {"id": "3a889791-1565-4765-bc9d-61b8730b9d20", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost, service, working capital, visibility, and compliance benefits"}, {"id": "0e78b8d2-e174-4dc0-8952-67baffd2b0e5", "type": "concept", "title": "ROI, total cost of ownership, and value realization"}], "description": "Students learn to connect system choices to strategy, service, cost, resilience, and growth."}]}, {"id": "5aa1b51a-6cbb-4b20-b7f0-94c3459c1e30", "type": "topic", "title": "ERP Foundations, Modules and Business Process Integration", "description": "ERP works by embedding business processes into shared modules and data structures. This unit gives students the operating map.", "children": [{"id": "237f1d75-df47-4e12-88be-80307fc4ff7a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Core ERP Modules", "children": [{"id": "0d879d50-ef46-4f71-bdef-abdd5e0be1ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Materials management, sales and distribution, production planning, warehouse management, finance, controlling, quality, and maintenance"}, {"id": "4a2131ad-7040-45fd-b7e7-c1cb916e81c9", "type": "concept", "title": "Module boundaries and handoffs"}, {"id": "9b052853-f9cd-4732-befb-c190e08b3656", "type": "concept", "title": "Transaction, master, and configuration data"}], "description": "Students learn the major ERP modules and the supply-chain work each supports."}, {"id": "5cee4b14-fc2b-4731-950f-bda863fb5ed5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Process Integration", "children": [{"id": "71b03f6b-f4b3-4bab-899c-805b3805c5e6", "type": "concept", "title": "Procurement to inventory to accounts payable"}, {"id": "ab7a6260-6a79-42b9-8269-3c7a65d28028", "type": "concept", "title": "Sales order to delivery to billing to receivables"}, {"id": "b803fc87-42f4-42ba-9c83-0192cf97f04f", "type": "concept", "title": "Production planning to shop-floor confirmation to inventory and costing"}], "description": "The point is to understand how one transaction triggers downstream operational and financial effects."}, {"id": "84791b65-e89e-47e6-bf32-43b32150b345", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ERP User Experience", "children": [{"id": "622344d8-a4d5-4647-8d7b-bcebf96b92bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Role-based interfaces, dashboards, workflows, approvals, and alerts"}, {"id": "a6b29035-16d1-42b9-bd84-559995818a68", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobile, Fiori-style, and low-code experiences"}, {"id": "77baf6e0-66c9-47ce-8c95-b2f4c414a900", "type": "concept", "title": "Usability, training, and adoption barriers"}], "description": "Students learn how users interact with modern ERP systems."}]}, {"id": "81f4fd55-3f59-4bab-98aa-7b40ea39f580", "type": "topic", "title": "Business Process Modeling and Systems Analysis", "description": "A good ERP course needs process thinking. Students learn how to map current work, design future work, and translate process needs into system requirements.", "children": [{"id": "9c705460-fdea-4603-a56b-ccd2fcdcb1ec", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Process Modeling", "children": [{"id": "37090ac7-1e8d-4387-99c8-e73ab6c21c37", "type": "concept", "title": "BPMN, swimlanes, SIPOC, value-stream maps, and process decomposition"}, {"id": "cd2d2b69-8a62-4abe-acf4-c369ff346e2f", "type": "concept", "title": "As-is and to-be models"}, {"id": "66c2e67f-0dc1-4314-98ae-9ec91b2ef52c", "type": "concept", "title": "Exceptions, handoffs, bottlenecks, and control points"}], "description": "Students learn visual tools for making supply-chain processes explicit."}, {"id": "37c61767-e45c-436c-9614-0718d2d92b4f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Requirements and Fit-Gap Analysis", "children": [{"id": "8c9e1e02-8275-4d9f-b8d7-ac5de3d15b68", "type": "concept", "title": "Functional, data, reporting, security, and integration requirements"}, {"id": "82efc616-1756-4c9f-a1eb-fbe09d6bbebb", "type": "concept", "title": "Fit-gap workshops and acceptance criteria"}, {"id": "3aff225e-c572-4034-af45-0d45e213e1b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Standard process adoption versus customization"}], "description": "The goal is to decide where a system fits, where process changes are needed, and where configuration or extensions are justified."}, {"id": "62690b8a-818b-41ad-8d08-2ebc27f9f91f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Process Governance", "children": [{"id": "74adb2de-6838-417d-a422-adbcd0e6e1e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Process owners, data owners, super users, and IT partners"}, {"id": "6d3b5d36-dfcc-4fee-9251-b2bff9b8ed69", "type": "concept", "title": "Change control and design authority"}, {"id": "45b57dc8-b3fc-4859-90d8-4db3e2c865cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Documentation, training, and continuous improvement"}], "description": "Students learn that enterprise systems require process ownership and decision rights."}]}, {"id": "14473478-e90c-4b11-9059-b21507d41afb", "type": "topic", "title": "Master Data Management and Data Governance", "description": "ERP quality depends on data quality. This topic teaches the data structures and governance disciplines that keep supply-chain processes reliable.", "children": [{"id": "b33b16a1-b4e1-451c-9fdd-f7fe0aa2b4eb", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supply Chain Master Data", "children": [{"id": "17a5f459-23c5-4c72-a14b-66de8be3a5b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Material, item, SKU, vendor, customer, plant, warehouse, location, work center, routing, and BOM"}, {"id": "7ffc24b1-f720-469f-b84c-9f5b2c5bc776", "type": "concept", "title": "Units of measure, lead times, sourcing rules, prices, and tax data"}, {"id": "b0ae9af6-f39e-4e17-a80e-8e2f66408ee8", "type": "concept", "title": "Data dependencies across modules"}], "description": "Students learn the master records that drive planning, execution, and finance."}, {"id": "ef37c226-86e0-44a5-a5f3-80dcf70b2df0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data Quality and Stewardship", "children": [{"id": "e8b09fe6-41fa-45da-a341-40992723175c", "type": "concept", "title": "Completeness, accuracy, timeliness, uniqueness, and consistency"}, {"id": "292a8ebe-57c0-4bd3-b64c-ba41a53c56aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Data owners, stewards, approval workflows, and data lifecycle"}, {"id": "1ef4c734-ce16-4b69-b3b4-651decb3586c", "type": "concept", "title": "Duplicate, obsolete, and conflicting records"}], "description": "The point is to prevent bad data from becoming bad operations."}, {"id": "80342ffc-21ff-41f4-b049-cddbc18d1d93", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Governance and Controls", "children": [{"id": "e1ad9f52-ae2d-4250-918b-a8099a27389d", "type": "concept", "title": "Master data policies and standards"}, {"id": "cc90f16f-77f1-4e99-9a57-e7d7d9d4c3e7", "type": "concept", "title": "Change logs, approvals, and segregation of duties"}, {"id": "feb5d890-720f-4b2c-b0ee-36126f063332", "type": "concept", "title": "Data lineage, metadata, and audit readiness"}], "description": "Students learn how governance makes data trustworthy and auditable."}]}, {"id": "0597f46f-6e2e-4793-bbb2-fd0f8e5393da", "type": "topic", "title": "Material Requirements Planning and Supply Planning Logic", "description": "MRP is one of the classic supply-chain uses of ERP. Students learn how demand, BOMs, inventory, and lead times become planned orders.", "children": [{"id": "c97e9fcb-1e3e-4848-bad9-4667a629097b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "MRP Inputs", "children": [{"id": "da163b7b-9dd8-4a6c-bbd1-b07e026edde5", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand forecasts, customer orders, BOMs, inventory balances, scheduled receipts, and lead times"}, {"id": "63682792-b874-4e05-87f7-7694b837dcb3", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning calendars, lot sizes, safety stock, and sourcing rules"}, {"id": "41dca6b2-f1db-44e9-aae2-3e340c00cb82", "type": "concept", "title": "Data errors and planning nervousness"}], "description": "Students learn what information the planning engine needs before it can produce useful recommendations."}, {"id": "01cb0db9-8d03-441b-8bb6-d5669b365e26", "type": "subtopic", "title": "MRP Calculations", "children": [{"id": "ea948860-916b-4c9f-a894-4024a543e322", "type": "concept", "title": "Net requirements, BOM explosion, time phasing, offsetting, and pegging"}, {"id": "49156f3c-b690-42b8-a134-1dc16e7cf779", "type": "concept", "title": "Planned orders, purchase requisitions, production orders, and exception messages"}, {"id": "2ad2c701-a27a-4a3c-86c3-8d05118e8e3f", "type": "concept", "title": "MRP versus DRP and multi-echelon planning"}], "description": "The goal is to understand the planning logic rather than treat ERP output as magic."}, {"id": "0db175e8-0a87-4241-a8e0-5703c5e6f7c8", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Planner Decision Making", "children": [{"id": "22d783c3-7605-4121-a1ef-2a63d3b156ce", "type": "concept", "title": "Expedite, defer, cancel, and reschedule messages"}, {"id": "1a85dd3b-b0b8-4ba2-921a-0810f5e825a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Shortages, excess, substitutions, and capacity checks"}, {"id": "ef478689-51a9-4072-8b8b-d07bf9b63ce5", "type": "concept", "title": "Planner workbenches and exception-based planning"}], "description": "Students learn how planners interpret and override system suggestions."}]}, {"id": "1ea362d0-cd77-4f2a-8d13-55ed1f97986e", "type": "topic", "title": "Procure-to-Pay and Supplier Integration", "description": "Procure-to-pay connects sourcing, buying, receiving, inventory, quality, and finance. Students learn the end-to-end process and the controls around it.", "children": [{"id": "fa97a213-d90a-40fc-a1d9-e3bf8a0a51ba", "type": "subtopic", "title": "P2P Workflow", "children": [{"id": "5daa4048-31f1-483e-a1f8-67d858f4c324", "type": "concept", "title": "Purchase requisition, purchase order, approval, goods receipt, quality inspection, invoice receipt, and payment"}, {"id": "6a5ba963-6784-4294-8b05-4381bcacd668", "type": "concept", "title": "Three-way match and tolerance management"}, {"id": "ae7f245c-309f-4948-85e6-6d9f300b5173", "type": "concept", "title": "Service procurement and indirect spend variants"}], "description": "Students learn the standard transaction chain from need to payment."}, {"id": "e82dcc79-f828-4733-b7c7-121365c7b005", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supplier Collaboration", "children": [{"id": "c94bb48a-644a-4625-a223-6f8cb1252621", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier portals, EDI, ASN, order acknowledgment, and vendor-managed inventory"}, {"id": "4dc234a9-6fe9-4649-85e6-303543a6cafd", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier scorecards and compliance documentation"}, {"id": "1fa1e534-3596-4363-bf03-2eb7a6a788ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Catalogs, contracts, and e-procurement"}], "description": "The point is to understand how ERP extends across organizational boundaries."}, {"id": "232090b4-9393-4ba4-958f-2e0ade0d955a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Controls and Risks", "children": [{"id": "6aede2ba-03f3-478a-ad8b-b2dbd862bd27", "type": "concept", "title": "Unauthorized purchases, duplicate payments, price variance, receipt errors, and fraud"}, {"id": "61b1c4d7-9ba2-4917-8cc6-8f85454646a2", "type": "concept", "title": "Approval matrices, delegation of authority, and audit trails"}, {"id": "2facf4a4-5716-4dd5-ab04-2ddf037aff75", "type": "concept", "title": "Segregation of duties among request, approve, receive, and pay"}], "description": "Students learn why P2P is a major internal-control area."}]}, {"id": "0593b1ff-691c-4d4e-9f0e-f75933f6a59a", "type": "topic", "title": "Order-to-Cash, Customer Fulfillment and Service", "description": "Order-to-cash links demand capture, availability, logistics, billing, and customer service. It is where ERP touches revenue and customer experience.", "children": [{"id": "c2e15f42-b4ef-44df-b60c-81338ff5a69d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "O2C Workflow", "children": [{"id": "ec653aca-ea35-4e99-9ce5-7b7056eff08c", "type": "concept", "title": "Quote, sales order, credit check, ATP, pick, pack, ship, invoice, and cash application"}, {"id": "382b191a-7628-4fd1-a52f-1bcd5116d495", "type": "concept", "title": "Backorders, substitutions, allocations, and delivery blocks"}, {"id": "12add95d-89bb-44ba-9275-455a00420562", "type": "concept", "title": "Returns, claims, and customer service cases"}], "description": "Students learn the end-to-end order process."}, {"id": "fb72b25a-01c3-4440-87a0-ecd6857dc31d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Availability and Fulfillment", "children": [{"id": "e3e4526f-35c6-401a-8b99-22c9e6da755b", "type": "concept", "title": "Available-to-promise, capable-to-promise, allocation, and reservation logic"}, {"id": "e97c6207-0726-451d-9760-77a196f6cc92", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer priority, service levels, and channel rules"}, {"id": "c83d42d3-0318-4f84-9114-dd79e1620eac", "type": "concept", "title": "Warehouse and transportation execution links"}], "description": "The focus is how system logic determines what customers can be promised."}, {"id": "1a7eaeaa-3df1-4180-a795-a760a6db4551", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revenue and Control Touchpoints", "children": [{"id": "c615c899-ec65-423d-bcad-6bf23d1771d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Billing, taxes, rebates, revenue recognition touchpoints, and credit management"}, {"id": "ee1ca0a5-37dc-4f90-ba5c-2609965c6157", "type": "concept", "title": "Order holds, pricing conditions, and discount approvals"}, {"id": "7279b493-7cd4-41f8-b633-d7bd9f13c55d", "type": "concept", "title": "Audit trail from order to cash"}], "description": "Students learn how operational transactions connect to financial results."}]}, {"id": "5df039eb-bfab-4f0a-a505-dd9f9642ecce", "type": "topic", "title": "Manufacturing Planning, MES and Quality Integration", "description": "ERP supports manufacturing by connecting materials, capacity, production, quality, and costing. Students learn how planning becomes shop-floor execution.", "children": [{"id": "3be416fb-d985-4f9a-bf98-75167845293f", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Production Planning", "children": [{"id": "23b17e50-2d9d-4e7b-9f77-f769db16a858", "type": "concept", "title": "MPS, MRP, routings, work centers, capacity, and production orders"}, {"id": "29fcf0a0-659e-4249-9892-f5c6e8609cc6", "type": "concept", "title": "Make-to-stock, make-to-order, assemble-to-order, and engineer-to-order"}, {"id": "14decd0e-b2a5-4023-b8be-a07d9fb0840d", "type": "concept", "title": "Finite versus infinite capacity and constraint visibility"}], "description": "Students learn the planning structures used in manufacturing environments."}, {"id": "bd432a90-c80d-4c8e-a64d-053e8f0716d5", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Shop-Floor Execution", "children": [{"id": "b1957c6f-6c7b-40d8-9451-1f08fb2fbdf7", "type": "concept", "title": "MES, confirmations, labor, machine time, scrap, yield, and downtime"}, {"id": "87724539-b428-4a73-a783-45ede520ea38", "type": "concept", "title": "Component issue, backflush, and finished-goods receipt"}, {"id": "34845180-ac42-4583-9e9a-0306bfc07a1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Traceability and genealogy"}], "description": "The point is to understand how production data flows back into the enterprise system."}, {"id": "b0f3d034-140d-4601-bfe5-b498cef300f2", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Quality and Cost Integration", "children": [{"id": "eb48d7a2-ea59-47a2-b0ba-4c5cd6bb94e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Inspection lots, nonconformance, corrective action, and holds"}, {"id": "35e3a560-e4b0-459d-9781-b20f0baf00d1", "type": "concept", "title": "Standard cost, variance, work-in-process, and production settlement"}, {"id": "5ef6d953-69bb-43c6-809a-11a72cbbd4cd", "type": "concept", "title": "Quality data for suppliers and customers"}], "description": "Students see how quality and costing are embedded in operational flows."}]}, {"id": "dedb1242-a27b-404c-9a5a-81438069b8ea", "type": "topic", "title": "Warehouse, Inventory and Logistics Systems", "description": "ERP supply-chain execution depends on warehouse and logistics systems. This topic connects WMS, TMS, inventory accuracy, and physical flow.", "children": [{"id": "d0aa0d7a-dd36-4613-be82-1c1c6ecc4603", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Warehouse Management Systems", "children": [{"id": "b15c136d-785b-4eaa-bca7-11d742de554b", "type": "concept", "title": "Receiving, putaway, slotting, replenishment, picking, packing, shipping, and cycle counting"}, {"id": "cebe48ca-5527-4485-b3a3-484fdccea4cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Barcode, RFID, mobile scanning, automation, and labor management"}, {"id": "1bb04dea-305b-4e4f-a5c7-f4c8fd01120e", "type": "concept", "title": "Warehouse tasking and exception handling"}], "description": "Students learn how WMS functionality supports execution."}, {"id": "b0eec975-23fd-4ef1-8d34-a34917f57a19", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Inventory Accuracy and Visibility", "children": [{"id": "c7d8e007-36ce-401e-b3bb-37937aa9ef73", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory status, batch, serial, lot, bin, and location control"}, {"id": "edfc909c-031e-4937-bc85-a253ebe1eac3", "type": "concept", "title": "Cycle counting, adjustments, reconciliation, and shrink"}, {"id": "e71d7311-693a-4c77-b412-481a510dc609", "type": "concept", "title": "Inventory valuation and financial impact"}], "description": "The goal is to connect system inventory to physical inventory."}, {"id": "1c5a9f70-4cac-4c6f-a500-7a316e2ad146", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Transportation and Yard Integration", "children": [{"id": "75d1e8b7-0a62-430c-b846-ba5fce8a9dc9", "type": "concept", "title": "TMS rating, tendering, shipment planning, tracking, freight audit, and claims"}, {"id": "639cea45-1dbb-4733-ac1a-5a2b3e92cd93", "type": "concept", "title": "Yard management, dock appointments, and trailer visibility"}, {"id": "b1c025e7-8c41-4af8-a446-ebce22eab432", "type": "concept", "title": "Carrier EDI/API and shipment event data"}], "description": "Students learn how logistics systems connect to ERP and WMS."}]}, {"id": "c1693132-51cd-4d12-aea5-8d9bb067736e", "type": "topic", "title": "ERP Analytics, BI and Supply Chain Control Towers", "description": "Systems are valuable only when they produce useful decisions. This section teaches reporting, dashboards, KPIs, and control-tower thinking.", "children": [{"id": "983c358a-4263-4b86-ab02-8972979f6267", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Operational Reporting", "children": [{"id": "efa4cad6-80ca-4576-a2f1-d474a42ccee2", "type": "concept", "title": "Open orders, inventory, shortages, aging, supplier performance, delivery performance, and exceptions"}, {"id": "dd0b8bde-eaac-4d93-b5d2-f1af8691d67a", "type": "concept", "title": "Embedded analytics and self-service BI"}, {"id": "3bde1eb7-6da3-4127-9b44-a3cd9d066683", "type": "concept", "title": "Report governance and metric definitions"}], "description": "Students learn the difference between transaction reports, management reports, and analytical views."}, {"id": "48de6c08-25eb-4554-9fe5-333ea4cfefc4", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Supply Chain KPIs", "children": [{"id": "53a746c0-8dcb-49c5-b392-0f3d375db369", "type": "concept", "title": "OTIF, fill rate, forecast accuracy, inventory turns, days of supply, schedule adherence, procurement savings, and order cycle time"}, {"id": "fedcc45f-2dc4-4b4f-88ec-b244c91d1245", "type": "concept", "title": "Leading versus lagging indicators"}, {"id": "e239bca6-97ca-4068-b9e9-2054dd9a680b", "type": "concept", "title": "KPI ownership, thresholds, and review cadence"}], "description": "The point is to choose measures that support action."}, {"id": "cbd07e64-7698-4fdf-9b6a-28dbe7eb0612", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Control Towers and Decision Support", "children": [{"id": "aeb6958d-833f-4edb-9e5b-4dc6eb265b42", "type": "concept", "title": "Visibility platforms, event management, alerts, predictive ETA, and risk signals"}, {"id": "05305b0b-6e6b-4412-9c2b-816e16cac410", "type": "concept", "title": "Scenario analysis and what-if planning"}, {"id": "2e485e9f-79a9-4fe1-af08-e7455d3c504e", "type": "concept", "title": "Decision rights and escalation workflows"}], "description": "Students learn how integrated data supports real-time coordination."}]}, {"id": "d042a3ba-8b97-48f6-bd8c-bf6bcc026a99", "type": "topic", "title": "Integration, APIs, EDI and Platform Architecture", "description": "Supply-chain systems rarely stand alone. Students learn how ERP connects to partners, platforms, machines, and analytics environments.", "children": [{"id": "49bf130e-2722-462e-8a2e-bcdde71fa1da", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Integration Patterns", "children": [{"id": "de6e22c9-bdec-4372-8147-3f027565c401", "type": "concept", "title": "Batch, real-time, API, EDI, file transfer, message queues, and event streams"}, {"id": "93464402-9cab-4af8-9e8b-46a45d15eeea", "type": "concept", "title": "Point-to-point versus middleware and iPaaS"}, {"id": "5219f643-ec0f-47c9-b0b4-0ec5e6dcbafe", "type": "concept", "title": "Canonical data models and mapping"}], "description": "Students learn the common ways enterprise systems exchange data."}, {"id": "ae14ae94-c256-4cb5-8105-f65ecc82e691", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Partner and Ecosystem Integration", "children": [{"id": "b9f98353-8eac-4a01-b6de-90f9188fb232", "type": "concept", "title": "Purchase orders, ASNs, invoices, forecasts, inventory, shipment status, and remittance data"}, {"id": "335553c8-3791-4902-ba0d-9642b725be6c", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier portals, customer portals, and logistics platforms"}, {"id": "9e95a6a9-d4ae-4b5e-8941-c6aa0155e36f", "type": "concept", "title": "Standards, testing, and onboarding"}], "description": "The focus is on supplier, customer, carrier, and marketplace connections."}, {"id": "2d824e26-86e3-4369-b1d1-a9fa23369b92", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Architecture Risks", "children": [{"id": "343377d3-cba8-40bd-93f0-366e95d46313", "type": "concept", "title": "Latency, failed messages, duplicates, reconciliation, and error handling"}, {"id": "8cca5d1b-5022-4644-bcaa-0354dda85952", "type": "concept", "title": "Interface monitoring, logging, retry logic, and support ownership"}, {"id": "9d672831-ee6b-4da7-a081-b96885a124cc", "type": "concept", "title": "Security, authentication, authorization, and data exposure"}], "description": "Students learn why integration design affects reliability and cyber risk."}]}, {"id": "280d310b-c5a6-4323-a6dc-41858ee47d9a", "type": "topic", "title": "Cloud ERP, SaaS and Digital Supply Chain Platforms", "description": "Enterprise systems increasingly run in cloud and SaaS environments. Students learn the architectural, operational, and strategic implications.", "children": [{"id": "a9e0d2d6-54ea-49b5-860f-a5adfe12aa1e", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cloud ERP Models", "children": [{"id": "d69de76a-4fc0-4c79-bbad-503821403264", "type": "concept", "title": "Public cloud, private cloud, hybrid, SaaS, and managed services"}, {"id": "43c53cc7-5723-4e3c-92a9-b00573c0ba7c", "type": "concept", "title": "SAP S/4HANA Cloud, Oracle Cloud ERP/SCM, Dynamics 365, NetSuite, and best-of-breed platforms"}, {"id": "e7cddcca-20d9-4dd3-90ca-58213944a994", "type": "concept", "title": "Upgrade cadence, extensibility, and vendor lock-in"}], "description": "Students compare deployment models and their trade-offs."}, {"id": "0d4f52b5-d369-4c51-bed6-4705c8236ba6", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Platform Capabilities", "children": [{"id": "fabb06ed-eb90-4b91-94e7-bddde00e7a2c", "type": "concept", "title": "Workflow automation, low-code apps, process mining, embedded analytics, AI services, and integration services"}, {"id": "deb22b3b-1314-4a49-96a1-543e1e1e247f", "type": "concept", "title": "Mobile, role-based, and API-first design"}, {"id": "c272b271-91bd-4f8b-94c8-335c13b0b996", "type": "concept", "title": "Data lakes, lakehouses, and operational data stores"}], "description": "The goal is to see modern ERP as a platform, not just a transaction system."}, {"id": "279a5f0a-ae5a-4d32-9092-3983f9867e21", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cloud Operations", "children": [{"id": "2452c097-c8f5-4127-a742-2f548454d44e", "type": "concept", "title": "Availability, backup, disaster recovery, observability, and incident management"}, {"id": "708ce793-8c5d-41c9-839d-2ab1c37a2d06", "type": "concept", "title": "Identity, access, and environment management"}, {"id": "bd20dcd1-90d0-47ab-9f30-a7e6db28e182", "type": "concept", "title": "Cost management, licensing, and service-level agreements"}], "description": "Students learn operational disciplines for cloud enterprise systems."}]}, {"id": "e33f1253-5952-49c5-b497-294cce54fd2f", "type": "topic", "title": "ERP Implementation, Project Governance and Change Management", "description": "ERP implementation is a business transformation project. This topic teaches the governance, delivery, testing, and adoption work needed for success.", "children": [{"id": "b1f44fc0-e4f1-4c25-982f-071dee9c2591", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Implementation Life Cycle", "children": [{"id": "5ca5359c-75bf-43bb-99d9-9ff4c41c5f54", "type": "concept", "title": "Discovery, blueprint/design, build, test, deploy, stabilize, and optimize"}, {"id": "5a8ccbd7-6cfb-44c4-9010-966573d616e9", "type": "concept", "title": "Waterfall, agile, hybrid, and fit-to-standard approaches"}, {"id": "d3423b67-000e-487b-8f22-efd049cc59b7", "type": "concept", "title": "Project charter, scope, plan, RAID log, and governance structure"}], "description": "Students learn major delivery phases and artifacts."}, {"id": "66563a68-b3f7-42e4-8c43-73d13056268d", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Testing and Cutover", "children": [{"id": "d50a1fdd-2a95-43f2-a216-93b24d264baa", "type": "concept", "title": "Unit, integration, user acceptance, regression, performance, and security testing"}, {"id": "8de41696-7aee-4e08-90d8-2d7af7b44133", "type": "concept", "title": "Mock cutovers, data migration rehearsal, and go/no-go criteria"}, {"id": "db17852e-6c06-4d9f-b9f9-b9e99e3daa9e", "type": "concept", "title": "Hypercare, issue triage, and stabilization"}], "description": "The point is to reduce go-live risk through disciplined validation."}, {"id": "8cc13fe8-e4a2-4f19-917e-7165a361af5c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Organizational Change", "children": [{"id": "1ba054de-48bb-40e9-ad38-444584133823", "type": "concept", "title": "Stakeholder analysis, communication, training, super-user networks, and resistance management"}, {"id": "ff02cca4-c540-4226-b04e-ac8ee9a6a3c6", "type": "concept", "title": "Role redesign and process ownership"}, {"id": "2cfd5072-b9d4-4015-9b11-f65fa886a6bb", "type": "concept", "title": "Benefits tracking and value realization"}], "description": "Students learn why user adoption is as important as system configuration."}]}, {"id": "195b242f-1932-4534-b2cf-d64b78eb0047", "type": "topic", "title": "Data Migration, Testing and ERP Process Labs", "description": "Hands-on process exercises make ERP concrete. Students learn to move data, execute transactions, and validate end-to-end flows.", "children": [{"id": "ad8c5353-8f22-429a-a9fb-c92105de7917", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Data Migration", "children": [{"id": "a5e6ef60-7ca3-45a2-9963-709e6a98a7bc", "type": "concept", "title": "Extract, cleanse, transform, load, validate, and reconcile"}, {"id": "f76a791c-404b-4be3-8251-1da86f7c4dc1", "type": "concept", "title": "Master data, open transactions, balances, and historical data"}, {"id": "c6a91fd5-846b-486d-a45b-d312825c6e50", "type": "concept", "title": "Migration defects and remediation"}], "description": "Students learn the practical discipline of moving legacy data into ERP."}, {"id": "4762a56f-ae71-4b68-b011-d4517206f051", "type": "subtopic", "title": "End-to-End Process Labs", "children": [{"id": "83e0ea4a-b3b8-46a5-b2dc-be75d24038d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Material creation, purchase order, goods receipt, invoice, sales order, delivery, and billing"}, {"id": "289c2c7f-5fd2-4455-9230-dd96329af75a", "type": "concept", "title": "MRP run, production order, warehouse task, and inventory count"}, {"id": "af50505d-b3cb-4f27-993d-50f726f87902", "type": "concept", "title": "Error diagnosis and exception resolution"}], "description": "The goal is to practice processes as integrated workflows."}, {"id": "94b477e2-ee33-4a0a-80e1-ce4bb5f61e5a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Test Evidence and Documentation", "children": [{"id": "6b7b8342-ffbb-40a6-88e6-4a4636c21a88", "type": "concept", "title": "Test scripts, test data, defects, retesting, approvals, and evidence"}, {"id": "71ce401e-a01b-4790-b5dd-60c3c278a9ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Traceability from requirements to tests"}, {"id": "529f1da5-9244-4e27-b132-c42e8e91e091", "type": "concept", "title": "Standard operating procedures and training aids"}], "description": "Students learn how ERP teams prove readiness."}]}, {"id": "39124d22-9b28-414a-980d-3f97e2ddcb7d", "type": "topic", "title": "Internal Controls, Segregation of Duties and Auditability", "description": "ERP systems sit at the heart of operational and financial controls. Students learn how controls are designed, monitored, and audited.", "children": [{"id": "be0c2017-4d3e-43eb-8f11-d146ce8b583a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Access and Authorization", "children": [{"id": "9704218b-5e34-4234-a3ab-8551b5538367", "type": "concept", "title": "Role-based access control, least privilege, privileged access, and emergency access"}, {"id": "dc36b30e-2122-4d2e-8b64-7fcd0557e408", "type": "concept", "title": "User provisioning, approval, review, and termination"}, {"id": "6339a451-336e-4dd4-8836-ce4eb9266cc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Authentication, MFA, and identity integration"}], "description": "Students learn the control logic behind user roles and permissions."}, {"id": "f1cd4295-aed2-4816-ade4-f5470742b203", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Segregation of Duties", "children": [{"id": "cc950ffb-1bf4-4633-abd9-07b485b6ba1e", "type": "concept", "title": "Create vendor and pay vendor"}, {"id": "5748e22d-e616-4b18-8847-6b67b738c54d", "type": "concept", "title": "Create purchase order and approve receipt"}, {"id": "e6b14efb-971d-4fb0-a97f-ecce9e0730f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Create customer, approve credit, and issue refund"}], "description": "The focus is on preventing risky combinations of access."}, {"id": "3a170aa0-c104-43f1-8e0c-5f002d70a763", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Audit and Compliance", "children": [{"id": "12a53e6c-0122-4bb4-89fd-50bff84a97d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Change logs, workflow approvals, transaction trails, and configuration records"}, {"id": "b388f303-b456-477a-af81-fdc566f66685", "type": "concept", "title": "SOX-style controls, IT general controls, and application controls"}, {"id": "b2e37f01-51c6-459a-acd3-5bd4d781a2bd", "type": "concept", "title": "Continuous controls monitoring"}], "description": "Students learn how ERP evidence supports internal and external assurance."}]}, {"id": "9568433e-05e8-426f-9467-b907d055c64c", "type": "topic", "title": "Cybersecurity, Privacy and Supply Chain Technology Risk", "description": "Enterprise systems create cyber and operational risk. This unit teaches security and risk management for ERP and connected supply-chain platforms.", "children": [{"id": "8a6d8512-9250-44e2-956e-0d6ec05e07ef", "type": "subtopic", "title": "ERP Security Threats", "children": [{"id": "95698935-0b9b-4cf2-83ae-c8eb5f5e4fcc", "type": "concept", "title": "Credential compromise, privilege abuse, ransomware, data exfiltration, interface abuse, and third-party compromise"}, {"id": "bad87ae6-af70-4833-9150-2fb1a3d1fd7d", "type": "concept", "title": "Misconfiguration, unpatched systems, insecure APIs, and shadow integrations"}, {"id": "c7e03bfe-d92e-4dbd-b6dd-c716c039da39", "type": "concept", "title": "Business interruption and fraud risk"}], "description": "Students learn common risk scenarios in enterprise systems."}, {"id": "50ae17ed-1ffa-4dd7-8616-50a923654137", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cyber Supply Chain Risk Management", "children": [{"id": "0e7ab1f1-3799-4c26-9737-4c523080bf26", "type": "concept", "title": "Supplier assurance, software risk, vendor access, and dependency mapping"}, {"id": "8cd37fa6-c7da-4bda-825c-f0581c8d1178", "type": "concept", "title": "Contractual security requirements and monitoring"}, {"id": "6b516dbe-9c2c-434a-9730-dee439ad2b0a", "type": "concept", "title": "Incident response and resilience planning"}], "description": "The goal is to apply frameworks such as NIST SP 800-161 to supplier and technology ecosystems."}, {"id": "a7cf8782-a074-4cd7-b52f-1117c5799b8c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Privacy and Data Protection", "children": [{"id": "f55d9713-c513-40fa-8502-f3608003738d", "type": "concept", "title": "Customer, employee, supplier, and payment data"}, {"id": "6db05f6a-19b0-4ab2-b935-66040c509278", "type": "concept", "title": "Data minimization, retention, masking, encryption, and lawful use"}, {"id": "d4ee44e3-19b7-4cf8-a5d2-926139d417ca", "type": "concept", "title": "Cross-border data and compliance considerations"}], "description": "Students learn how personal and sensitive data must be governed in ERP contexts."}]}, {"id": "dc4ff381-d027-468d-9a80-05415e9b4e04", "type": "topic", "title": "Advanced Planning, AI, IoT and Automation in ERP-Enabled Supply Chains", "description": "Modern supply chains combine ERP with advanced planning, AI, IoT, automation, and digital twins. This topic prepares students for the next layer of systems capability.", "children": [{"id": "5d195183-9918-4908-948e-8322d4c07b47", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Advanced Planning Systems", "children": [{"id": "7a3e6896-a42a-4d4b-a5e6-c6ae1a6634aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Demand planning, supply planning, S&OP, inventory optimization, and allocation"}, {"id": "b45d4d48-cdcd-4214-b69e-bf42b9e6f89f", "type": "concept", "title": "Constraint-based planning and scenario simulation"}, {"id": "e9c14794-6b92-4d70-be59-3e9bbcb30155", "type": "concept", "title": "Planning master data and integration to execution"}], "description": "Students learn how planning systems extend core ERP."}, {"id": "9743a002-97c6-401c-9d47-3875d19aefc9", "type": "subtopic", "title": "AI and Predictive Analytics", "children": [{"id": "5cf6d623-258a-47bd-b80e-457e772371d6", "type": "concept", "title": "Forecasting, anomaly detection, ETA prediction, supplier risk, and recommendation engines"}, {"id": "feb4efb0-4e1e-42a5-9943-58938d30972c", "type": "concept", "title": "Model evaluation, bias, explainability, and human oversight"}, {"id": "9a1c2a56-8f54-4ba5-b80d-47f19f616db4", "type": "concept", "title": "Operationalizing analytics into workflows"}], "description": "The point is to understand useful AI applications and their data requirements."}, {"id": "ad16c1c3-a381-4292-93cd-e4338b84d77a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "IoT and Automation", "children": [{"id": "6716ea7a-45c5-46e3-bde3-de3cf2d684cf", "type": "concept", "title": "Sensors, RFID, telematics, robotics, automated storage, and machine data"}, {"id": "629ef220-97ed-4a4a-988b-e7e11aab93ec", "type": "concept", "title": "Digital twins and real-time asset visibility"}, {"id": "c212388f-95dc-4698-ac76-178b5809e50f", "type": "concept", "title": "Automation governance, safety, and exception handling"}], "description": "Students learn how physical operations generate digital signals."}]}, {"id": "c6705bbd-d9f9-4bf1-b36d-5a7a32440123", "type": "topic", "title": "Capstone ERP Process Exercise and Digital Transformation Case", "description": "The course ends with a practical ERP-enabled supply-chain case. Students diagnose a process, configure or simulate the flow, analyze data, and recommend a transformation plan.", "children": [{"id": "620c54dc-f061-491c-95ae-a6fb9b245e29", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Case Diagnosis", "children": [{"id": "bc75508b-0b19-427b-bc71-c195eaa6efc4", "type": "concept", "title": "Process map, pain points, data issues, controls, integrations, and stakeholders"}, {"id": "1fb4d44b-8da4-4a69-bd80-d0625a076e97", "type": "concept", "title": "Current-state performance and risk evidence"}, {"id": "fbed6276-167a-4f4e-9c79-4fde3a95ca6d", "type": "concept", "title": "Decision criteria and scope boundaries"}], "description": "Students begin by identifying the business problem and system/process constraints."}, {"id": "2f3d4233-c898-4170-803d-309a881eced3", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Solution Design", "children": [{"id": "4fcf8ab7-65cd-432a-bd8f-f889ff5d915a", "type": "concept", "title": "To-be process, system roles, master data changes, integration needs, dashboards, and controls"}, {"id": "4460458c-0683-4801-94b1-cd005438519a", "type": "concept", "title": "Implementation plan, training, testing, cutover, and change management"}, {"id": "71ca9e6c-8fb6-4238-95d4-deceebaf1092", "type": "concept", "title": "Cybersecurity, governance, and data-quality considerations"}], "description": "The capstone asks students to design an integrated, realistic improvement."}, {"id": "a2924bd5-44a3-483c-92c5-cb520d604e87", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Executive Recommendation", "children": [{"id": "05989c7c-d4e0-44b1-84b8-e99fc0aadf37", "type": "concept", "title": "Business case, expected benefits, risk mitigation, timeline, and operating model"}, {"id": "87fedeff-bce7-45e9-a4c5-119ab2cfc5d2", "type": "concept", "title": "KPI dashboard and value realization plan"}, {"id": "72889d23-9138-4102-a2df-ecadf353c9b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Lessons learned from the ERP process exercise"}], "description": "Students present a decision-ready transformation argument."}]}], "dbBacked": true}$scerpjson$::jsonb,
